# Cute DevOps Patterns! — local copy

The pattern library that informs how this system is built and operated, mirrored
here by the `osahris.cute_devops.patterns` Ansible role so people and agents can
read it without network access.

- **[Patterns! 🔷](patterns.md)** — `patterns/`: how we prefer to do things, and
  why. Categories: `about/`, `workflows/`, `development/`, `operation/`, `meta/`.
- **[Anti-Patterns! 🔻](anti-patterns.md)** — `anti-patterns/`: practices that
  look reasonable and aren't, each pointing at what to do instead.

Read them with anything that reads markdown:

```bash
ls {{ patterns_dest }}/patterns/
grep -ril worktree {{ patterns_dest }}/patterns/
```

This directory is **read-only in practice** — Ansible overwrites it on every
run, and entries that disappear upstream are pruned from here. To change a
pattern, change it in the `cute-devops` repository and let the deploy carry it
back.

Upstream: <https://cute-devops.patterns.how>

